<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heart of Darkness</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1899">1899</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Heart of Darkness is a novella by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-conrad">Joseph Conrad</a>, published in serial form in 1899 and as a book in 1902. Narrated by the seaman Marlow, it describes a journey up an African river to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> agent Kurtz, drawing on Conrad's own voyage up the Congo in 1890. It is among the most widely read and debated works on European imperialism.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heart-of-darkness.jpg" alt="Heart of Darkness" width="320" height="493" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William Blackwood (Life time: November 20, 1776 – September 16, 1834) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blackwood%27s_Magazine_-_1899_cover.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
